Lab 06 — Image Segmentation

Point, line and edge detection, gradients, Canny, Hough transform and thresholding, implemented with OpenCV, NumPy, Matplotlib and scikit-image.

Open In Colab

Replace YOUR_USERNAME and YOUR_REPO in the badge link with your GitHub username and repository name.

Overview

Image segmentation partitions an image into meaningful regions.

Discontinuity-based methods detect abrupt changes (points, lines, edges).
Similarity-based methods group pixels with similar properties (thresholding).

This notebook walks through both approaches with experiments and lab tasks.

Lab Outcomes
Explain image segmentation and intensity discontinuities
Use intensity differences to highlight abrupt changes
Detect points, directional lines and edges using spatial operators
Compare first- and second-derivative responses near a noisy edge
Compute gradient magnitude and orientation
Apply the Canny edge detector and analyze its parameters
Detect line segments using the Hough transform
Compare global, Otsu and adaptive thresholding
