Key Observations
Differentiation amplifies noise, so Gaussian smoothing is applied before derivatives. Second derivatives are affected the most.
Textured regions produce many false edge responses.
Canny thresholds control the trade-off between weak-edge detection and false edges.
Hough parameters (threshold, minLineLength, maxLineGap) control missed versus false line detections.
Under uneven illumination, adaptive thresholding performs better than global or Otsu thresholding.
